  "openSourceLicenses": "Open-source licenses",
  "permissionsTitle": "Permissions and device notes",
  "permissionsBody": "The app uses the camera torch, screen brightness, haptics, and — only when Shake to toggle is on — the motion sensor. On Android, background shake monitoring runs in a foreground service with a persistent notification. The app does not request internet, location, camera images, microphone, or contacts.",
  "volumeButtonsTitle": "Volume buttons",
  "volumeButtonsBody": "Android and iOS reserve the volume buttons for system audio and accessibility. Flash Light Pro does not intercept them, because that would require accessibility or root access, which this app does not request.",
  "iosLimitationsTitle": "iOS integration",
  "iosLimitationsBody": "On iOS, the Shake to toggle and Shortcuts actions work while the app or the system intent is running. iOS does not offer Android-style Quick Settings tiles or home screen widgets for unrestricted background flashlight control. iOS also suspends app execution and releases the torch when the app leaves the foreground, so there is no background flashlight mode.",
  "madeOffline": "The flashlight works offline. Ads need a connection.",
  "privacyPolicyTitle": "Privacy policy",
  "privacyIntro": "Flash Light Pro works on your device. The flashlight itself needs no account and no network. The free version shows ads from Google AdMob, and an optional one-time purchase removes them.",
  "privacyViewOnline": "View full policy online",
  "privacyLocalTitle": "Data stored on your device",
  "privacyLocalBody": "Preferences such as language, default mode, brightness, and shake sensitivity are stored locally by the operating system. Ad frequency limits, your ad consent choice, and Remove ads purchase status are cached locally too. The Android Quick Settings tile and home screen widget also store the last torch state locally so they can show the correct state.",
  "privacyHardwareTitle": "Hardware access",
  "privacyHardwareBody": "The app uses the camera flash (torch) and screen brightness. It reads the accelerometer only while Shake to toggle is enabled: in the foreground, and on Android through a foreground service with a persistent notification when you leave the app. It does not capture camera images, microphone audio, location, contacts, or photos.",
  "privacyAdsTitle": "Advertising",
  "privacyAdsBody": "The free version may show banner, native, interstitial, and app-open ads from Google AdMob. Ads are requested only after the consent required in your region, and never while a light is active or an update is required. You can review your choices with Privacy options in Settings. The Remove ads purchase stops all ads on this account.",
  "privacyBillingTitle": "Remove ads purchase",
  "privacyBillingBody": "Remove ads is a one-time, non-consumable purchase handled by Google Play or the App Store. The app never receives your payment details. The entitlement is cached on your device and confirmed with the store, and you can restore it at any time from Settings.",
  "privacyNoAnalyticsTitle": "No analytics or crash uploads",
  "privacyNoAnalyticsBody": "The app includes no analytics SDK and no remote crash reporting. Google AdMob may collect device and ad-interaction data under Google's own privacy terms. The flashlight, SOS, strobe, Morse, and screen light keep working without a connection.",
  "privacyPolicyFooter": "This policy applies to Flash Light Pro version {version}. On iOS the app requests motion access, and only when Shake to toggle is enabled. On Android 13 and later it asks for notification permission so the background flashlight and shake services can show their controls. Ads and purchases are provided by Google AdMob and the platform store under their own privacy terms.",
